  "id": "cross-modal-transfer",
  "term": "cross-modal transfer",
  "definition": "Cross-modal transfer is the carrying of information from one sensory modality to another, such as using what is heard to guide responses to what is seen. In this context, it refers to recognizing the same emotional information across different senses.",
